  "description": "Soroban settings upgrade sets, one per target protocol, applied after the single protocol upgrade: first 'enable', then the protocol's network set. Each .xdr file is the base64 of one XDR ConfigUpgradeSet (as vendored upstream; some end in a newline, which is not part of the base64); the .json next to it is its upstream source. upgrade_set_sha256 is the hash of the decoded bytes (the ConfigUpgradeSetKey content hash). Protocols 1 to 19 have no Soroban settings and need none; Protocol 20 has no upstream set (quickstart's files start at p21), so no bring-up targets it.",
